8 and g8 are currently safe), so castling is legal.\n\nReason:  \nCastling is one of the most important opening principles. **K: e8-g8** offers immediate king safety, enables rook activation, and is time-efficient. There is no urgent threat from White that requires a defensive pawn push or piece interposition. Black has sufficient control over the center and development is behind — castling addresses that. No checks or immediate threats prevent it, and the move is both safe and strategic.\n\nAnswer: K: e8-g8"}
